// Into a fossil cave by its east mouth: under the skull resting on the east wall, up onto the beast lying
// on the floor (its ribs bedded in a mound of rock, each standing just proud of it), west over the ribs,
// S at the rope ladder's head on the mound's west end, down to the chest, unhurt, with nothing crumbling or
// falling. No wall climbing: the mound's east face (about 2.2 m) is beyond a jump, so the mole takes the rope
// gun up it: every 200 ticks the script throws the hook into the cave's roof just ahead, walks 25 ticks, climbs
// with W+A (rolling off onto the mound at its top), then jumps (letting go of a rope it didn't need).
// Before (Hampus 13:50, "beast on the floor"): the skeleton and the scaffold hung 3 m over the floor and
// came down on a mole walking under them, about 11 m from the west wall.
map
